# Mobile UI Testing Rules

## Device Management

- One device type per CI shard (iOS simulator, Android emulator)
- Boot devices before test suite, shut down after
- Use cloud device farm (BrowserStack, Saucelabs) for physical device coverage
- Set explicit timeouts — mobile tests are slower than web

## Gesture Testing

- Use framework-native gesture APIs, not coordinate-based swipes
- Test scroll then tap patterns (lazy-loaded content)
- Test keyboard dismiss before form submission

```typescript
// Detox — gesture API
await element(by.id('list')).swipe('up', 'fast', 0.5);
await element(by.id('submit-button')).tap();
```

## Native Interactions

- System alerts (permissions, push notifications): handle in setup
- Deep links: test both cold start and warm start
- Background/foreground: test app state restoration
- Orientation: test critical flows at portrait and landscape

## Performance Budget

- Screen transitions: < 500ms
- List scroll: 60fps
- App cold start: < 2s
